    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d596">

                <pb facs="0647" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg597"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr.
                            Taylor.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-09-12"><hi rendition="#italic">September 12,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 186.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge receipt of your No.
                    227, of the 27th ultimo, and to approve your course in demanding of the Spanish
                    Government permission for the return of the missionaries to the Caroline
                    Islands.</p>
                <p>The draft for $17,500 which accompanied your No. 209, of July 13 last, was duly
                    received.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
